      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T23:17:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The master GPIO spreadsheet indicates this signal needs an internal pull-up. Having the internal pull-up prevent taking interrupts in a case where interrupts were enabled on this line but the sensor wasn\u0027t configured. But, that\u0027s not a case we would expect as we always initialize the sensors prior to enabling the interrupts.\n\nI don\u0027t think we should edit generated.dta for this change. My take is we should leave this as is for now. The CL that adds fan support has a TODO added to this file to reflect that the EE team is going to review the master GPIO spreadsheet and make sure the values are correct.\n\nUntil that point, I think we make manual edits to this file for cases where functionality will be broken (eg output is configured as open drain, but needs to be push-pull for control the signal level, or a build error because of a missing enum)",
      "parentUuid": "187e74b4_004ff5cd",
